  "body": "## What happens\n\n`assets/posts/heidenhain-klartext.cps:297-301` refuses an arc when its start radius and end radius differ by more than 0.0001 mm. It compares values that are already rounded to 4 decimals. Rounding alone can give up to about 0.00028 mm of radius difference. So the post can refuse correct CAM arcs.\n\n## What the control allows\n\nThe machine parameters of the Fehlmann Picomax 55 (iTNC 530, NC 340490-03, the machine parameter file from the delivery CD) have **MP 7431 = 0.016 mm**, the tolerance for the circle end point. The post is 160 times stricter than the control.\n\n## Expected\n\n- The check uses the control's arc tolerance (a machine-file value, default 0.016 mm for this machine), with a margin, and compares unrounded or consistently rounded values.\n- A refused arc still names the radii and the limit.\n\n## Done means\n\n- An arc with a radius difference of 0.0003 mm after rounding posts.\n- An arc above the machine's tolerance is still refused by name.\n- Tests pin both cases. The existing Klartext goldens do not change.",
